 Marvel trivia to share at your  next dinner party  however the admission that stars  character for me Incredible Hulk and the  spider-man movies are the same person  arguably puts a tiny wrinkle in the  overall Marvel Canon particularly  regarding a tie-in novel that  accompanied the release of The  Incredible Hulk as many fans have noted  the Incredible Hulk novelization takes a  different approach to the character star  played in the film identifying him as  being a korean-american genius named  Amadeus Cho who was first introduced in  Marvel Comics in 2005 since star is  definitely not korean-american like Cho  is the two characters are more like  analogues to one another than anything  else but we digress in the novel version  of the story Banner meets show when he  sneaks into the computer lab finding the  students studying for his final exams  much like movie bana does with martin  stars character bana offers chosen pizza  and that's the end of that a scene like  this was actually supposed to be  included in the movie as an extended  version of stars actual scene in the  final film the deleted scene sees bana  trying to trick his way into the lab  with the promise of free pizza with the  excuse that someone in the radiation lab  called for it and then bailed the tactic  works like a charm  getting Banner easy access to use the  computer and search for the data he  needs you my friend are a hero  interestingly enough the Cho character  referenced in a novelization actually  ended up with a meaty role in Marvel  Comics years later going on to succeed  banner as the Hulk as the star of the  2015 comic series the totally awesome  Hulk the connection between Martin stars  Incredible Hulk character and the books  Amadeus Cho is pretty undeniable but  since Feige has since stated that a  computer nerd in the Incredible Hulk  movie is actually Roger Harrington that  means he's not armored Deus Chow so in  case you were wondering that means that  the Incredible Hulk n